How it works:
- `addFileImports` resolves each path with `ctx.getFullPath`, which respects `__cwd`. It appends the resolved paths to `__resultImports` and returns the paths as the LLM provided them.
- `appendFunctionSetters` writes one `@import !file {path}` tag per queued path on the `> result` message, then clears the var.
- `__resultImports` is skipped when writing setter lines, so it never shows up as an assignment in the result message.
- The next flatten sees the `@import` tags on the result message and loads them through the normal import flow. Globs work because `!file` implies `!merge`, and duplicates are handled by the existing `importedModules` check.

One limitation: `parseBaseConvoImport` splits the import value on spaces, so paths containing spaces will not import correctly.


