The imported messages are inserted at the index of the message that holds the `@import` tags, so they end up before it. For a top-level import that is the right place. For `> result` and `> endFileImport` messages, though, the content lands before the tool call in the flattened conversation.

The fix is to insert imports after the message for those two roles. The insertion index also advances after each import, so files keep the order of their tags.

